  "kanji": "布",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 布\ntitle: cloth; distribute\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 巾\nradicalNumber: 50\nonyomi: [フ, ホ]\nkunyomi: [ぬの, し.く, きれ]\ndistractors: [市, 師, 希]\n---\n\n# 布 — cloth; distribute\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 巾 (no. 50) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n布 concerns cloth and, in other words, spreading or distribution. The native noun 布 ぬの is cloth or fabric, while 配布 はいふ means distribution. 毛布 もうふ means blanket and 財布 さいふ means wallet; their modern objects need not be made from one particular traditional material.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice the crossing upper strokes over 巾 and imagine a piece of cloth hanging below them. This is a shape-based memory aid, not a verified origin.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| フ | on | [毛布](../words/毛布.md) もうふ - blanket |\n| ホ | on | 布衣 ほい - linen kariginu; historical robe |\n| ぬの | kun | [布](../words/布.md) ぬの - cloth; fabric |\n| し.く | kun | Source-only reading. JMdict indexes 布く しく - promulgate; lay railway tracks; deploy troops (search-only kanji form); this index form is not a recommended word example. |\n| きれ | kun | 布地 きれじ - fabric; cloth |\n\nKANJIDIC2 also records `し.く`. No suitable non-index word example was established in the inspected JMdict snapshot. These are character-dictionary readings for lookup, not recommendations to use this kanji as an everyday spelling of a word.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [分布](../words/分布.md) ぶんぷ - distribution across an area\n- [布](../words/布.md) ぬの - cloth; fabric\n- [毛布](../words/毛布.md) もうふ - blanket\n- [財布](../words/財布.md) さいふ - wallet; purse\n- [布団](../words/布団.md) ふとん - futon; Japanese bedding\n- [座布団](../words/座布団.md) ざぶとん - floor cushion; ふとん becomes ぶとん in the compound\n- 配布 はいふ - distribution\n\n## Notes\n\n- 布衣 ほい is a historical clothing term, not a general recommendation for naming modern clothes. Here kariginu names a type of robe.\n- The きれ row is demonstrated inside 布地 きれじ, also spelled 切れ地. 布地 also has the separate reading ぬのじ, fabric or cloth; do not assume that every 布地 is read きれじ. The linked standalone 布 article teaches ぬの.\n- The 布く しく form is search-only in the inspected JMdict spelling record. The entry notes this spelling specifically for promulgating, laying railway tracks and deploying troops (senses 3, 5 and 6), not its futon example. 敷く is the entry's primary spelling. 布く remains lookup evidence, not an ordinary spelling recommendation.\n- JMdict labels the whole spelling 布団 as ateji, a spelling in which ordinary character meanings need not explain the word. That label alone does not establish the historical role of each individual character.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1291980, 1296970, 1473190, 1496840, 1496890, 1497020, 1504160, 1533950, 1591910, 2247550, 2859268.\n",
